From 9535025421da27ffa6f406516dda6d28481551df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: velle <velle2386@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:39:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 62/65] fix(render): the render clock stops while no frame is
 drawn

The engine draws when the compositor sends a frame callback, and none
come while the wallpaper is covered; it also stops drawing while it
pauses for a fullscreen window. g_Time was the wall clock, so the first
frame after either stepped engine.frametime, every timeline animation
and every particle system by the whole wait: a script fading over a
second of frametimes finished in that one frame, and particles were
simulated for minutes in one step.

FrameClock moves the render clock by one frame when a frame comes more
than half a second after the last, or before it (the wall clock is the
system clock and can be set back). It also keeps the first frame's step
at zero, which the static timeStarted flag did before.

Proof: a fixture whose script logs any frametime over 0.5 s, frozen
with SIGSTOP for 10 s on a headless rig: the previous build logs
"frametime 10.023", this one nothing.
